Moonsilence wrote:
> 1. What is the difference between stealth and invisibility?

If you are stealthy, monsters won't hear you (you won't wake them up
unless you kick down doors or step on squeaky boards or things like
that). If you are invisible, monsters won't see you (they will attack
squares next to you (because they think you're there) or not notice
you at all).


> 3. Does it make a diffenece if my pet attacks peaceful/tame monsters? 
> For example, if I play an orcish char, the game promts me wether I 
> really want to attack the o. My pet just does... How can I make him 
> stop doing that?

You can't, but you don't have to. You don't get any penalties for your
anything your pet does.


> He even attacks watchmen in mine town.

Ok, that can be annoying, because those watchmen tend to just kill your
pet. Just lock the watchmen (or your pet) in some empty room.


> This game is hard enough

There are actually people in this group who would not agree with you on
that. I don't think the game has to be made easier.


> Death 
> trough starvation because I just didn't happen to search in the right 
> place first and ran out of time... Survival in the early game 
> shouldn't depend on that. Crap.

That's a matter of skill/experience with the game, actually. I almost 
never die of starvation anymore.


> A shopkeeper angered in an earlier game will remember my name and just 
> start attacking me. Now there is no more point in using the same name. 
> Arggg! It doesn't make sense, just because I used the same name, 
> doesn't mean I'm the same char. Can't the shopkeeper remember that he 
> has already killed me in that earlier game, so I can't be the same guy 
> even if the name is the same, and move on with his life?

You're not the same char, but you're still the same player. I think this
feature is there so that on a system with multiple players other players
don't have to deal with the shopkeepers you angered when they run into
your bonesfile, but you still do.


> 7. How do I select a secondary weapon? In the official guidebook, it 
> only says that x swaps secondary with primary, but not how to select a 
> weapon in order to do so.

wB x wA
Where B is the weapon you want to be secondary and A is the weapon you
want to be primary.


> 8. What's the difference between peaceful and tame monsters?

Peaceful monsters won't attack you, tame monsters are your pets.


> Can I 
> aquire one as a pet?

Tame monsters already are your pets. Peaceful monsters can be made tame 
just like non-peacefuls:
For dogs, cats and horses: Throw food they like (meat for cats and dogs,
vegetables for horses)

For every monster:
- Read a scroll of tame monster (the monster might resist)
or
- Sit on a magic trap while the monster is near you (of course a magic
   trap can have several other bad effects, so this isn't the easiest/
   safest way to get a pet)


